I added a fast path that fetches the field at the course-point profile's known index for the favorite field (index 7) and only falls back to the original linear `GetField(8)` scan if that slot isn't field 8, making the common case a single indexed lookup instead of an 8-field scan.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsFavoriteValid() const
    {
        // Fast path: in the course point profile the favorite field (num 8)
        // is the last field, so a direct indexed access avoids the linear
        // field-number scan performed by GetField().
        const Field* field = GetFieldByIndex(7);
        if( FIT_NULL != field && 8 == field->GetNum() )
        {
            return field->IsValueValid();
        }

        // Fallback preserves exact behaviour for any other field layout.
        field = GetField(8);
        if( FIT_NULL == field )
        {
            return FIT_FALSE;
        }

        return field->IsValueValid();
    }
```